---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { SUB_PROCESSORS } from "../constants/legal";
---

<Legal title="Privacy" description="Which companies receive your data when you use EliseLAB, and what each one receives.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="notice" role="note">Draft. The legal wording on this page is still to be written and approved. The sub-processor list below is factual.</p>

  <h2>Sub-processors</h2>
  <p>EliseLAB sends some of your data to the companies below. Each one receives only what its row says.</p>

  <ul class="processors">
    {
      SUB_PROCESSORS.map((processor) => (
        <li>
          <h3>{processor.name}</h3>
          <p>{processor.purpose}</p>
          <p><strong>Receives.</strong> {processor.receives}</p>
          <p><strong>Never receives.</strong> {processor.neverReceives}</p>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h2>Your own Claude</h2>
  <p>A Scan runs on your computer, in the Runner, with your own Claude account. EliseLAB does not send your code to a model provider. Anthropic is your provider, not ours.</p>

  <h2>Signals</h2>
  <p>Signals are on for every account. An account admin can turn them off in Account settings. Turning them off stops new requests to TypeSafe.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p class="pending">Wording pending approval.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p class="pending">Wording pending approval.</p>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>EliseLAB has no delete button for an account. To delete yours, ask Lynkfire Limited at the contact address below. A person there does it by hand.</p>
  <p>Deleting an account removes its members, repositories, Scans, Findings, comments, stored reports and uploaded zips.</p>
  <p>Stripe keeps its own payment records under its own policy.</p>
  <p class="pending">Wording pending approval. The owner confirms the list above and how fast a request is handled.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p class="pending">Wording pending approval.</p>

  <h2>Last updated</h2>
  <p class="pending">Date pending approval.</p>
</Legal>
